WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.398 --> 00:00:19.552
I forgotten to close my curtain, so the full moon woke me.

2
00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:24.998
As I stretched out my arm toward the curtain, a scream split the night.

3
00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:27.000
What a cry!

4
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:33.284
It came from the third floor, and my heart stood still as I heard a fierce struggle in

5
00:00:33.304 --> 00:00:34.505
the room above my own.

6
00:00:34.525 --> 00:00:36.807
"Help! Help!"

7
00:00:37.348 --> 00:00:39.550
a half-smothered voice called above me.

8
00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.272
"Rochester! Come!"

9
00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:46.756
the voice cried while the staggering and stamping went on wildly.

10
00:00:47.897 --> 00:00:51.780
A door opened on my floor, and then someone rushed along the corridor.

11
00:00:52.921 --> 00:00:56.264
Another foot stamped on the floor above, and something fell.

12
00:00:57.476 --> 00:00:59.317
At last there was silence.

13
00:01:00.558 --> 00:01:06.261
I threw on my robe, and though horror shook my limbs, went out into the darkened corridor, where

14
00:01:06.401 --> 00:01:08.802
all the guests were gathering and speaking at once.

15
00:01:08.822 --> 00:01:10.623
"Who's hurt?"

16
00:01:10.643 --> 00:01:13.125
"Are there robbers?"

17
00:01:14.145 --> 00:01:14.705
"Where's Mr.

18
00:01:14.766 --> 00:01:17.227
Rochester?" "Here I am!"

19
00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:22.550
Mr. Rochester descended the stairs from the third floor, carrying a candle.

20
00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.392
Blanche Ingram ran to him and seized his arm.

21
00:01:27.572 --> 00:01:29.354
"What awful event has taken place?"

22
00:01:29.374 --> 00:01:32.937
"A servant had a nightmare," he replied.

23
00:01:32.957 --> 00:01:34.578
"It's nothing.

24
00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:37.401
You must all return to your rooms now."

25
00:01:38.522 --> 00:01:40.704
I went back to my room, but I didn't sleep.

26
00:01:41.845 --> 00:01:47.409
Instead I dressed carefully and sat on the edge of my bed, waiting for I knew not what.

27
00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:50.632
At last someone tapped on my door.

28
00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:52.434
"Are you awake?"

29
00:01:52.814 --> 00:01:54.696
Mr. Rochester asked softly.

30
00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.442
I opened my door, and there he stood with a candle.

31
00:01:58.462 --> 00:02:01.805
"Do you have a sponge and some smelling salts?"

32
00:02:02.245 --> 00:02:02.866
he whispered.

33
00:02:04.007 --> 00:02:05.908
I nodded and fetched them from my room.

34
00:02:06.949 --> 00:02:08.871
He beckoned me to follow him upstairs.

35
00:02:10.852 --> 00:02:15.196
Outside a door he paused and said, "Do you turn sick at the sight of blood?"

36
00:02:15.216 --> 00:02:18.839
"I don't think so, but I haven't been tested."

37
00:02:18.859 --> 00:02:22.442
"Give me your hand because we can't risk a fainting fit."

38
00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:24.784
I put my fingers in his.

39
00:02:26.084 --> 00:02:28.126
"Warm and steady," he remarked.

40
00:02:28.586 --> 00:02:33.129
Inside the room a tapestry had been looped up on one side to reveal a door to another

41
00:02:33.169 --> 00:02:33.830
room beyond.

42
00:02:35.031 --> 00:02:38.413
I heard a snarling, dog-like sound coming from within.

43
00:02:38.433 --> 00:02:41.055
"Wait here," said Mr.

44
00:02:41.095 --> 00:02:43.316
Rochester as he went into the inner room.

45
00:02:44.517 --> 00:02:50.502
A shout of laughter greeted his entrance, followed by Grace Poole's goblin-like, "Ha-ha!"

46
00:02:51.702 --> 00:02:53.504
Then I heard a low voice address him.

47
00:02:54.724 --> 00:02:55.305
Soon Mr.

48
00:02:55.365 --> 00:02:58.027
Rochester came out and closed the door behind him.

49
00:02:59.148 --> 00:03:03.852
He directed me to the other side of some closed curtains, which concealed a large bed.

50
00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:07.375
A man sat in a chair next to the bed.

51
00:03:09.156 --> 00:03:14.981
His eyes were closed, but I recognized the pale and seemingly lifeless face of Mason.

52
00:03:16.202 --> 00:03:20.626
I saw too that one sleeve and one side of his shirt were almost soaked in blood.

53
00:03:20.646 --> 00:03:23.252
"Hold the candle," Mr.

54
00:03:23.312 --> 00:03:26.814
Rochester directed me as he began to sponge Mason's wounds.

55
00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:29.356
"Am I in immediate danger?"

56
00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:30.616
murmured Mason.

57
00:03:30.636 --> 00:03:32.998
"It's a mere scratch, Richard.

58
00:03:34.038 --> 00:03:36.920
I'll fetch a doctor for you, and you'll be on your way by morning."

59
00:03:38.061 --> 00:03:42.683
Mr. Rochester explained that he might be gone for an hour or two and that I was to

60
00:03:42.743 --> 00:03:44.024
sponge Mason's wounds.

61
00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:49.187
If the man felt faint, I was to put a glass of water to his lips and the

62
00:03:49.227 --> 00:03:50.648
smelling salts to his nose.

63
00:03:51.808 --> 00:03:54.230
"You're not to speak to each other," warned Mr.

64
00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.891
Rochester. "Do you understand?

65
00:03:58.132 --> 00:03:59.473
No conversation."

66
00:04:01.294 --> 00:04:05.436
And so he left the room and locked the door, and I was alone with Mason.

67
00:04:06.597 --> 00:04:10.259
How had this quiet stranger become involved in this web of horror?

68
00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:13.801
Why was he up here when I'd clearly heard Mr.

69
00:04:13.881 --> 00:04:15.762
Rochester assign him a room below?

70
00:04:16.983 --> 00:04:18.504
The night seemed to last forever.

71
00:04:19.688 --> 00:04:23.891
Sometimes I feared that Mason was dying, and I wasn't even allowed to speak to him!

72
00:04:25.111 --> 00:04:28.273
At last I heard Pilot barking outside, and Mr.

73
00:04:28.353 --> 00:04:30.054
Rochester returned with the doctor.

74
00:04:30.074 --> 00:04:32.736
"Now, good fellow, how are you?"

75
00:04:33.096 --> 00:04:33.616
asked Dr.

76
00:04:33.656 --> 00:04:38.099
Carter. "She tried to kill me," Mason replied weakly.

77
00:04:38.119 --> 00:04:39.820
"What's this?"

78
00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:40.821
said Dr.

79
00:04:40.841 --> 00:04:43.622
Carter, examining the wound in Mason's shoulder.

80
00:04:43.642 --> 00:04:45.984
"This wasn't done with a knife."

81
00:04:47.156 --> 00:04:49.998
"She bit me when Rochester got the knife away from her.

82
00:04:51.079 --> 00:04:51.960
It was frightful."

83
00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.061
Mason shuddered.

84
00:04:54.081 --> 00:04:59.125
"I told you to be on your guard when you went near her," said Mr.

85
00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:03.528
Rochester. "You should have waited until tomorrow and had me with you.

86
00:05:04.589 --> 00:05:05.249
Hurry, Carter.

87
00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:09.052
The sun will soon rise, and I must get him away from here."

88
00:05:10.132 --> 00:05:14.876
Mr. Rochester ordered me to go downstairs and fetch a clean shirt and Mason's cloak.

89
00:05:15.944 --> 00:05:17.565
Then, with the assistance of Dr.

90
00:05:17.586 --> 00:05:21.389
Carter, Mason walked downstairs and out to a waiting coach.

91
00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.271
Dr. Carter climbed in after him.

92
00:05:25.412 --> 00:05:27.654
Mason looked out the window and addressed Mr.

93
00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:30.796
Rochester. "Let her be taken care of.

94
00:05:31.877 --> 00:05:33.358
Let her be treated tenderly.

95
00:05:34.459 --> 00:05:38.202
Let her He stopped, overcome by tears.

96
00:05:38.222 --> 00:05:41.185
"I do my best," said Mr.

97
00:05:41.225 --> 00:05:46.773
Rochester. As the coach rolled away, he added, "I wish there were an end to this!

98
00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.115
Come walk with me, Jane."

99
00:05:50.276 --> 00:05:54.979
In the garden he gathered a rose, the first of the season, and offered it to me.

100
00:05:54.999 --> 00:05:58.361
"Thank you, sir," I said.

101
00:05:59.502 --> 00:06:02.464
Then I asked, "Will Grace Poole still live here?"

102
00:06:02.484 --> 00:06:04.346
"Oh yes!

103
00:06:05.566 --> 00:06:06.867
Now put her out of your thoughts."

104
00:06:08.128 --> 00:06:09.609
But I had more questions.

105
00:06:09.629 --> 00:06:13.072
"Is the danger that you feared last night gone now?"

106
00:06:14.212 --> 00:06:18.136
"I cannot vouch for that until Mason is out of England, and not even then.

107
00:06:19.317 --> 00:06:24.281
He wouldn't knowingly hurt me, but with one careless word he might deprive me of happiness."

108
00:06:25.482 --> 00:06:28.525
We came to an arbor, and he urged me to sit next to him.

109
00:06:28.545 --> 00:06:35.171
"Suppose that long ago a man committed not a crime, but an error.

110
00:06:36.392 --> 00:06:40.396
Now he meets someone whose good and bright qualities he has sought for twenty years.

111
00:06:41.544 --> 00:06:44.705
Would it be all right for him to attach himself to her?"

112
00:06:45.865 --> 00:06:48.746
He looked eagerly at me, but I didn't know how to answer him.

113
00:06:49.906 --> 00:06:54.407
While around us the birds were singing and the leaves rustling, I stayed silent.

114
00:06:56.308 --> 00:06:58.249
Then abruptly his tone changed.

115
00:06:59.469 --> 00:07:01.930
"You've noticed my tender feelings toward Miss Ingram.

116
00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.270
Do you think she'd regenerate me if I married her?"

117
00:07:06.451 --> 00:07:07.351
I didn't respond.

118
00:07:07.371 --> 00:07:10.952
"Jane, you're quite pale from the night's excitement.

119
00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:13.822
Are you angry that I disturbed your sleep?"

120
00:07:14.962 --> 00:07:15.443
"No, sir."

121
00:07:15.463 --> 00:07:20.947
"Then perhaps you'll sit up with me the night before I'm married because I know I won't be

122
00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:21.728
able to sleep."

123
00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.510
"Yes, sir," I answered.

124
00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:27.532
"I'd like to be useful whenever I can."

125
00:07:28.793 --> 00:07:29.254
"Oh, look!

126
00:07:30.335 --> 00:07:31.816
Two of our guests are at the stables.

127
00:07:32.897 --> 00:07:34.258
Go quickly so they don't see you."

128
00:07:35.439 --> 00:07:40.343
As I went one way and he went another, I heard him saying cheerfully to the men, "Mason

129
00:07:40.383 --> 00:07:41.684
was up before you all today.

130
00:07:42.865 --> 00:07:44.368
I rose at four to see him off."
